diff --git a/ai/lessons.md b/ai/lessons.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..48b9b32
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ai/lessons.md
@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
+# Lessons
+
+Hindsight from building features in this app. The ADRs under `docs/adr/` are the
+intent; this is what was actually learned doing it.
+
+## Async CSV export (docs/adr/0001-async-customer-csv-export.md)
+
+- **`Loam::ProgressJob#result` is the parking spot for a job's output**, not just
+  a summary. Using it for the export CSV meant no migration and no new entity,
+  and it inherits tenant scoping — the download action is a plain `find`, and a
+  foreign id is a 404 for free.
+- **Reach for `Loam::Export.csv` even when the spec names three columns.** It
+  carries the policy read-filter, the `[encrypted]` redaction and
+  `Loam::Csv.safe`. A hand-written three-column CSV silently drops all three.
+- **`Loam::Export.csv` batches with `find_each`**, which discards any order on
+  the relation and logs a warning. Pass it an unordered scope (`by_status`
+  alone); the index's `.ordered` is for the screen, not the file.
+- **Watch substring assertions on seed data.** `active@acme.test` is a substring
+  of `inactive@acme.test`, so `assert_no_match` on a raw CSV body passes when the
+  filter is broken. Parse the CSV and compare values instead.
+- **Minitest 6 (Rails 8.1) ships no `stub`/`mock`** — `require "minitest/mock"`
+  raises LoadError. Swap a seam by hand with `define_singleton_method` and
+  restore it in an `ensure`, rather than adding a gem.
+- **A member must be refused over HTTP, not just shown no button.** Both the
+  start and the download actions carry `require_role!(:manager)`, and the tests
+  assert 403 on the request itself.
